PART A. THE AVDBCMS COMMUNITY LICENSE 1.0
------------------------------------------

1. What this license covers

   "AVDBCMS" in this license means the work of the AVDBCMS project in this
   package:
   - the code, themes, looks, texts and other files that AVDBCMS made;
   - the changes that AVDBCMS made to the files of the original open-source
     project that AVDBCMS is based on (the changes only, not the original
     code; see section 7 and Part B, section B1);
   - the AVDBCMS documentation (README.md, UPGRADE.md, CHANGELOG.md,
     COMMUNITY_SETUP_GUIDE.md and docs/).

   It does not cover third-party components. They keep their own licenses
   (see Part B and the file NOTICE).

2. What you may do

   Anyone may, free of charge:
   - use AVDBCMS, also for your own websites that earn money, for example with
     ads or premium plans (a website of your own company, or of an organisation
     that employs you or that you volunteer for without pay, counts as your own
     website; a customer's or client's website does not, even when you are paid
     to work on it: a contractor, freelancer or business that is paid to
     install, set up, run or change AVDBCMS for someone else is not using it
     for its own website);
   - copy AVDBCMS;
   - change AVDBCMS;
   - share AVDBCMS, changed or unchanged, under the conditions in section 4.

3. What nobody may do: sell AVDBCMS

   Nobody may ask for or take money, or any other payment, for:
   - copies or downloads of AVDBCMS;
   - changed versions of AVDBCMS;
   - AVDBCMS themes or looks, or any part of AVDBCMS;
   - installation packages that contain AVDBCMS;
   - access to copies of AVDBCMS (the software itself) behind a paywall (for
     example a paid download area or a paid membership that is needed to get
     AVDBCMS), or access to them that is only given in exchange for something
     else of value (for example watching ads, filling in paid surveys or
     passing through paid link shorteners);
   - installing, setting up or handing over AVDBCMS, or a changed version of
     it, for other people (for example a paid installation or setup service, or
     a website with AVDBCMS that is built for a customer and handed over);
   - support for AVDBCMS, or running, customizing or changing AVDBCMS or its
     themes for other people (for example paid support, paid management of
     someone else's AVDBCMS website, paid customization or paid changes; what
     counts as your own website is said in section 2);
   - hosting plans or other services that come with AVDBCMS installed or set
     up (a host whose customers install AVDBCMS themselves is fine).

   Charging for any of these counts as selling AVDBCMS. So does earning money
   with copies of AVDBCMS that you share, through money-making code or links
   built into them (section 4). Free help is available from the AVDBCMS
   community on Telegram:
     Telegram group: https://t.me/+jj6McO-iYfA0MTM1
     Telegram support (personal): https://t.me/avdbapi_support

   Allowed: running your own website with AVDBCMS and earning money with that
   website, for example with ads, premium plans or other paid areas of that
   website (section 2). The rules above are about AVDBCMS itself, not about
   the content of your website. You may also sell a website that you have
   really run yourself (its domain, content and audience), as long as AVDBCMS
   on it stays free under this license with every notice kept and no price is
   asked for AVDBCMS itself. Building or setting up AVDBCMS websites in order
   to sell them is not allowed.

4. Conditions when you share AVDBCMS

   When you share AVDBCMS or a changed version of it:
   - it must stay free of charge (section 3);
   - it must not carry money-making code or links of the person who shares it
     (or of anyone that person works with): no ads, affiliate or referral
     codes, paid or sold links (backlinks), cryptocurrency miners, or tracking
     whose data is sold to others, built into the copy. This is not about the
     notices and links that come with AVDBCMS itself (keep the notices), and
     running your own website with AVDBCMS, with your own ads on that website,
     stays allowed (section 2);
   - it must stay under this same license, and you must include this LICENSE
     file and the NOTICE file;
   - you must keep every copyright, license and source notice, including the
     MIT notice of the original project (Part B, section B1) and the license
     files of the third-party components;
   - you must mark your changes: say in the changed files, or in a list that
     comes with your copy, which files you changed.

5. No warranty

   AVDBCMS is provided "as is", without any warranty. The authors are not
   liable for any damage or loss that comes from using it.

6. End of your rights

   If you break this license, your rights under it end automatically. People
   who received AVDBCMS from that person keep their rights, as long as they
   follow this license.

7. The original MIT project, and copies from before 1.2.0

   AVDBCMS is based on an open-source project published under the MIT
   License (Copyright (c) 2024 Anton Bourtnik). The code of that project keeps
   the MIT License wherever it is in AVDBCMS, and its notice is kept word for
   word in Part B, section B1. For a file that contains code of that project,
   this license covers only what AVDBCMS added to it and changed in it.

   Before 1.2.0, AVDBCMS was tested in community test packages (12 to 23
   October 2026). They were not public releases, and their LICENSE file was
   the MIT License of the original project. A copy of such a package that
   someone already received keeps the license file it came with. This license
   applies from AVDBCMS 1.2.0.

8. Contributions

   If you send changes to the AVDBCMS project, you agree that they may be used
   and shared under this license.


