B2. Laravel and the PHP packages in vendor/

AVDBCMS runs on the Laravel framework (version 12, MIT License). The release
packages contain the PHP packages that Composer installs into vendor/;
composer.lock lists every one of them with its license. Each package keeps its
own license, and the license files that come with the packages stay in their
folders in vendor/. Most of them are under the MIT License. The others are:
- BSD-3-Clause: firebase/php-jwt, league/commonmark, league/config,
  nikic/php-parser, tijsverkoyen/css-to-inline-styles, vlucas/phpdotenv;
- Apache License 2.0: aws/aws-sdk-php, aws/aws-crt-php,
  giggsey/libphonenumber-for-php-lite, phpoption/phpoption (the two AWS
  packages carry a NOTICE file; NOTICE repeats it);
- GNU Lesser General Public License: dompdf/dompdf (LGPL-2.1),
  dompdf/php-font-lib (LGPL-2.1 or later), dompdf/php-svg-lib (LGPL-3.0 or
  later), ezyang/htmlpurifier (LGPL-2.1 or later);
- BSD-3-Clause, GPL-2.0 or GPL-3.0, as you choose: nette/schema, nette/utils;
- ISC: paragonie/sodium_compat.

The source code repository does not contain vendor/: Composer installs it from
composer.lock.

B3. JavaScript and CSS packages in the built files (public/build/)

The styles and scripts in public/build/ are built from the source code in
resources/ together with npm packages (package.json and package-lock.json name
them). Each package keeps its own license. Most of them are under the MIT
License, for example React, Preact, Bootstrap, Alpine.js and Chart.js. The
others are:
- Apache License 2.0: hls.js, Tom Select, React Aria and React Stately (with
  their @internationalized, @react-aria and @react-types packages),
  @swc/helpers and the @orchidjs packages;
- Font Awesome Free: icons under CC BY 4.0, fonts under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1, code under the MIT License;
- BSD-3-Clause: intl-messageformat, react-transition-group;
- 0BSD: tslib;
- Unlicense: tweetnacl.

The Font Awesome Free font files in resources/admin/lib/ (fa-brands.woff,
fa-regular.woff, fa-solid.woff) are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
resources/sass/normalize.scss starts with normalize.css 8.0.1 (MIT License),
which is built into public/build/ with the other styles.

B4. Package files in public/vendor/ and public/css/

public/vendor/ holds the browser files of Laravel Horizon (public/vendor/horizon/)
and of Log Viewer by opcodesio (public/vendor/log-viewer/), both under the MIT
License, and the tracker script of the Umami web analytics project
(public/vendor/umami/script.js; see NOTICE).

public/css/pdf.min.css, the style of the invoice PDFs (the same file is in
css/), is a build of Bootstrap 3.4.1 with normalize.css 3.0.3, both under the
MIT License; the file keeps their notices.

B5. FFmpeg in bin/ (full release package only)

The full release package (avdbcms-X.Y.Z.zip) contains ready-built FFmpeg
programs in bin/linux-x64/, bin/linux-arm64/ and bin/windows/: ffmpeg and
ffprobe, and on Windows also ffplay and the FFmpeg DLL files. AVDBCMS runs
them as separate programs, for example to read the length of an uploaded video
and to make thumbnails. They are not AVDBCMS work. They are licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3:
- bin/linux-x64/ and bin/linux-arm64/: static builds of FFmpeg 7.0.2 made by
  John Van Sickle (https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/). The license text is
  GPLv3.txt; readme.txt names the build and every library built into it.
- bin/windows/: an FFmpeg build of the FFmpeg source code at git revision
  b801f1fe6d (build N-124319-gb801f1fe6d-20260503), configured with
  --enable-gpl and --enable-version3. The license text is LICENSE.txt.

Keep these license and readme files whenever you share a package that contains
bin/. The FFmpeg project publishes the source code of FFmpeg, both release
7.0.2 and the git revision named above, at https://ffmpeg.org/download.html.
The update package (avdbcms-update-X.Y.Z.zip) does not contain bin/, and the
source code repository holds only bin/README.md there, not the FFmpeg programs.

